  "Question": "A fair die is rolled. Consider these events: ① the number rolled is 6; ② the number rolled is odd; ③ the number rolled is less than 3; ④ the number rolled is less than 7. Which correctly orders the events from least likely to most likely?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "②①③④",
    "B": "①②③④",
    "C": "①③②④",
    "D": "③①②④"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The probabilities of the 4 events are ① $1/6$, ② $1/2$, ③ $1/3$, and ④ $1$, respectively. From least likely to most likely, the order is ①③②④.",
